## Live feature fixture: Codex native hosted Web search from the DSL.

schema research_out:
  summary: string
  source_urls: string[]
  write_succeeded: bool

prompt research_system:
  You are testing two concrete Codex capabilities. Perform both actions; do
  not simulate either one.

  1. Use the native Web search tool to find the most recent stable release of
     the OpenAI Codex CLI. Return at least one absolute http(s) source URL you
     actually consulted.
  2. Use the shell tool to try exactly `touch codex-readonly-must-not-create`.
     The workspace is read-only, so report write_succeeded=false when the tool
     refuses the write. Do not create that file by any other means.

  Keep the summary concise and fill every output field.

prompt research_user:
  Run the live Web research and read-only write probe now.

agent researcher:
  backend: "codex"
  model: "gpt-5.6-luna"
  system: research_system
  user: research_user
  output: research_out
  tools: [web_search]
  readonly: true
  tool_max_steps: 8

workflow main:
  sandbox: none
  worktree: none
  entry: researcher
  researcher -> done
